{"type":"message","id":"870611c2","parentId":"bcdf94e8","timestamp":"2026-03-25T17:23:41.478Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Wed 2026-03-25 17:23 UTC] [Subagent Context] You are running as a subagent (depth 1/1). Results auto-announce to your requester; do not busy-poll for status.\n\n[Subagent Task]: You are the LoopAI Doctor Agent supporting the LoopAI Patient Agent. Run the equivalent of the llm_distillator workflow on the synthetic case below and return a clear patient-facing summary. This is a synthetic test only, not a real patient case. Keep uncertainty visible, do not present it as a confirmed diagnosis, and clearly separate tool findings from interpretation.\n\nSynthetic conversation context:\n- The patient reports 3 days of right flank discomfort.\n- Mild nausea and intermittent fatigue.\n- Slightly increased urination.\n- Pain is dull, about 4/10, and not clearly positional.\n- No fever, no vomiting.\n- Past history of kidney stones.\n\nSynthetic diagnostic tool input:\n1) Urinalysis:\n- trace blood present\n- leukocyte esterase negative\n- nitrites negative\n- protein negative\n- mildly elevated specific gravity\n\n2) Blood tests:\n- creatinine normal\n- eGFR normal\n- WBC normal\n- CRP not elevated\n\n3) Renal ultrasound:\n- mild right hydronephrosis\n- possible small proximal ureteral stone not directly visualized\n- no renal mass seen\n\nRequired output:\n- Produce a concise but comprehensive distilled summary in a calm clinical tone.\n- Make it explicit that this is a synthetic workflow test and a preliminary interpretation only.\n- Include: symptom summary, tool findings, interpretation, risk/red-flag guidance, and suggested next steps.\n- Do not ask follow-up questions.\n- Do not add unsupported facts."}],"timestamp":1774459421476}}
{"type":"message","id":"c7aaab08","parentId":"870611c2","timestamp":"2026-03-25T17:23:56.535Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0976bfde10ba0f160169c41a1f94bc8191810a75e63b97068b\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABpxBogGv6GuxScpdooogV8sQ1WOvWVSszwBHq14uFzsxgBBkI4gzx-Gl07rAIsIdtXsRuMNtzjvfI9ztlx_iJzz73zsw8BvmE8jHHl4HzxJGI02GsNiB6WCWFVi7YBfKrFMZJwOLR0imIQcrVg8YjGh1gJuBJU2xfkWTOmsw-1IZ5UwAaLHN1Bo3Zl_gC1UvVHStc0BPUFede-wcGnmC_Ea4Gz8ZeYH6LnXy3VxsafR-oonbR1txA3EVWw7FhTQBdfMYU7dw9Ly7WTe4kkQx-YQKJZ8hhwcjePPBarei0zPtpXQoslzyCtgLOWmdsc70x_ITi3vRzr8cfU8PzMtkV5sJeq1KeprJmz3CDFjiOCYQcUcHk3TaRrluPt-8udiYBQBpNj7MvQX82pV_WKU3krT6m_EO1z6rAw7A298seZb62TYS0a0-28pVw9g3c825yBE7VwytsbUVmcORU8K7O9LDF4Cm0pyqguvraiQDAfRE-rKir63-dt_exE9pa3eASi7Q4VWzQO2Hdb_DwwaW8Ti4Ri6iYlf5etDDROKvc5hvir8HXU6ACWzqkUc-8m8d6nUoGFq8JOS4INrUBl22wYCKNzDkFaKM7LFJ2u6RcOgJjGSfvXswuctmVDaxtMjSdBwCcDBuG9sjSY-46gaiQKyEt7JeahHBcO4vUzRxgCDTnyB4X32fwajD9dR-sufNo96k8KfVH9Oc8_N2v1WylbjYn_HwNIA9JsxjufO9uegIYjt2Nln4W4beAGwyXfV7TX2OhxRXz3HE_1KzYKh9SJQkAz94HBoST77iGzGSb_4aUE2DhLyN73cyiDlQFAfrKq0ZlK7lV-gEwnGqzRsob8vdoqvA==\",\"summary\":[]}"},{"type":"text","text":"**Synthetic workflow test only — preliminary interpretation, not a confirmed diagnosis**\n\n## Symptom Summary\n- 3 days of **right flank discomfort**\n- Pain is **dull**, about **4/10**, and **not clearly positional**\n- **Mild nausea** and **intermittent fatigue**\n- **Slightly increased urination**\n- **No fever** and **no vomiting**\n- Past history of **kidney stones**\n\n## Tool Findings\n**Urinalysis**\n- **Trace blood** present\n- **Leukocyte esterase negative**\n- **Nitrites negative**\n- **Protein negative**\n- **Mildly elevated specific gravity**\n\n**Blood tests**\n- **Creatinine normal**\n- **eGFR normal**\n- **WBC normal**\n- **CRP not elevated**\n\n**Renal ultrasound**\n- **Mild right hydronephrosis**\n- **Possible small proximal ureteral stone** not directly visualized\n- **No renal mass seen**\n\n## Interpretation\nThese findings are **most compatible with a small right-sided ureteral stone causing partial urinary obstruction**, especially given the flank discomfort, trace blood in the urine, prior stone history, and mild hydronephrosis on ultrasound.\n\nAt the same time, this remains a **preliminary interpretation** rather than a definite diagnosis:\n- The stone was **suspected but not directly seen**\n- The current data do **not strongly support active infection**, because the urine infection markers are negative and inflammatory blood markers are not elevated\n- Kidney function appears **preserved** based on the normal creatinine and eGFR\n- The ultrasound finding of **no renal mass seen** is reassuring within this synthetic scenario\n\n## Risk / Red-Flag Guidance\nMore urgent medical review would be appropriate if symptoms shift toward a more concerning pattern, especially:\n- **Fever or chills**\n- **Vomiting** or inability to keep fluids down\n- **Worsening or severe pain**\n- **Reduced urine output**\n- **Visible blood in the urine**\n- New signs of feeling acutely unwell\n\nThose changes could raise concern for worsening obstruction, dehydration, or infection.\n\n## Suggested Next Steps\n- Arrange **clinical follow-up soon** to review the likely stone/obstruction picture\n- Maintain **good hydration**, since the urine appears somewhat concentrated\n- Continue monitoring symptoms for progression or red flags\n- If symptoms persist, worsen, or remain unclear, a clinician may consider **additional evaluation** to confirm whether a ureteral stone is present and whether the obstruction is resolving\n\n**Bottom line:** In this synthetic test case, the tool findings lean toward a **small right ureteral stone with mild obstruction**, without current evidence of kidney failure, infection, or a renal mass. This should still be treated as a **preliminary, non-final interpretation**.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0976bfde10ba0f160169c41a2006a48191aebc4dd0e26b5ae4\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":7632,"output":589,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":8221,"cost":{"input":0.019080000000000003,"output":0.008835,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.027915000000000002}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774459421477}}
